<title>BELGIUM: Belgian March yr/yr inflation 1.46% vs 1.98% Feb.</title>
<headline>Belgian March yr/yr inflation 1.46% vs 1.98% Feb.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian Economics Ministry released the following data on inflation -</p>
<p>    BELGIAN CONSUMER PRICES     March	February   March 1996</p>
<p>    Index (base 100=1988)	 123.94     124.50     122.16</p>
<p>    Mth/mth change (in pct)	-0.45	-0.12	 0.07</p>
<p>    Yr/yr change (in pct)	   1.46	 1.98	 2.03</p>
<p>    Health index *		  121.31     121.88</p>
<p>    Mth/mth change (in pct)	-0.47	 0.17</p>
<p>NOTE - * excludes unhealthy products such as tobacco, alcohol and petrol, is used for inflation adjustments of rents and wages.</p>
<p>The ministry said it recorded no price rises in March, while the cost of fresh fruit and vegetables, fuels, foreign travel and plants and flowers all fell.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
